<h1>The Lord of the Rings</h1>

<a href="https://link.amazon/B0408WUVX" class="new-amazon-album-link">
<Image src={lr_book} alt="" />

Cover of The Lord Of The Rings book trilogy.
</a>

<p><strong><em>The Lord of the Rings</em></strong> is an epic fantasy novel written by the English academic <strong>J. R. R. Tolkien</strong>.</p>

<p>It remains one of the most popular works in <strong>20th-century literature</strong> and holds a special place as <strong>Enya's favourite book</strong>.</p>



<h2>A Journey Through Middle-earth</h2>

<p>The story of <em>The Lord of the Rings</em> takes place in the imaginary <strong>Third Age of Middle-earth</strong>.</p>

<p>These lands are populated by <strong>Men</strong> (humans) alongside several other humanoid races and fantastical creatures:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Hobbits</strong></li>
<li><strong>Elves</strong></li>
<li><strong>Dwarves</strong></li>
<li><strong>Orcs</strong></li>
</ul>

<p>The epic narrative centres on the corrupting <strong>Ring of Power</strong>, forged by the <strong>Dark Lord Sauron</strong>.</p>

<p>Starting from quiet beginnings in the <strong>Shire</strong>, the story ranges across Middle-earth and follows the <strong>War of the Ring</strong>.</p>

<p>These sprawling events are mostly witnessed through the eyes of the central protagonist, <strong>Frodo Baggins</strong>.</p>

<h2>A Lasting Cultural Legacy</h2>

<p>The immense and enduring popularity of <em>The Lord of the Rings</em> has led to numerous references across popular culture.</p>

<p>It continues to inspire artwork, music, video games, and subsequent literature.</p>

<p>Adaptations of the novels have been successfully translated for <strong>radio, theatre, and film</strong>.</p>

